  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nWhen navigating, often there is some state that is specific to the time of navigation that needs to be maintained across the different state, e.g.:\r\n- media playback position\r\n- state of internal iframes\r\n- state of a cross-document view transitions that affects how it is handled on the new state\r\n\r\nFor same-document navigations, this is nicely handled by the [`NavigateEvent.info`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/NavigateEvent/info) attribute. It is passed when calling e.g. `back()` and is readable in the `navigate` event handler. However, there is no such thing for cross-document navigations.\r\n\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nToday, custom info can be passed to another same-origin document via:\r\n- `sessionStorage`\r\n- the URL\r\n\r\nHowever:\r\n- `sessionStorage` is also shared with new windows and iframes, so it gets messy to use it for details that are only important for the navigation itself\r\n- The URL is too limited as it can't be used for history traversals, where the URL is already set.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nSuggesting add an `info` attribute to `NavigationActivation`. It would be writable on `pageswapEvent`, and readable from `window.navigation.activation`, in a structured-clone manner. \n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
